 {
  "id": "M14/p4",
  "lesson": "M14",
  "kind": "prediction",
  "prompt": "<p>Store the rank-16 truncated SVD of a <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>5000</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>768</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">5000 \\times 768</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">5000</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">×</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">768</span></span></span></span> matrix instead of the matrix: <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo>×</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>5000</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>768</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">16 \\times (5000 + 768 + 1)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">16</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">×</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">5000</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">768</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span> numbers instead of <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>5000</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>768</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">5000 \\times 768</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">5000</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">×</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">768</span></span></span></span>. About how many times smaller is it?</p>",
  "answer": "42",
  "answerKind": "numeric",
  "tol": 1,
  "options": [],
  "explain": "<p><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>3,840,000</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">/</mi><mn>92,304</mn><mo>≈</mo><mn>41.6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">3{,}840{,}000 / 92{,}304 \\approx 41.6</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">3</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span></span><span class=\"mord\">840</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span></span><span class=\"mord\">000/92</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span></span><span class=\"mord\">304</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">≈</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">41.6</span></span></span></span>. Multiplying a vector by the factors is cheaper by about the same ratio. LoRA uses exactly this to fine-tune a large model: the update to a <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>4096</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>4096</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">4096 \\times 4096</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">4096</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">×</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">4096</span></span></span></span> weight matrix is stored as two thin factors of rank 8 or 16.</p>"
 },
 {
  "id": "M14/p5",
  "lesson": "M14",
  "kind": "prediction",
  "prompt": "<p>You run PCA on embeddings whose mean vector is long compared with their spread, but forget to subtract the mean. What does the first component find?</p>",
  "answer": "a",
  "answerKind": "choice",
  "tol": 0,
  "options": [
   {
    "key": "a",
    "html": "<p>Essentially the direction of the mean: it explains the offset of the cloud from the origin, not its shape.</p>"
   },
   {
    "key": "b",
    "html": "<p>The same first component as with centring.</p>"
   },
   {
    "key": "c",
    "html": "<p>The direction of least variance.</p>"
   },
   {
    "key": "d",
    "html": "<p>Nothing: the SVD fails without centring.</p>"
